.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tokenbooth-daemon 1  "tokenbooth 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
tokenbooth\-daemon \- Run the daemon (started by systemd as the tokenbooth user)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtokenbooth daemon\fR [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the daemon (started by systemd as the tokenbooth user)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/tokenbooth/sock]
The daemon\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/pidvault.sock]
pidvault\*(Aqs control socket, which the daemon asks whether this shell is unlocked
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR [default: /var/lib/tokenbooth]
Keep each caller\*(Aqs state under this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_MOUNT>\fR [default: /run/pidvault]
Where pidvault shows unlocked vaults; each profile\*(Aqs key is kept in its vault there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
